# escape_gate_fomor -- the gate to the Fomoire, Balor's way (north-west). What it shows, and why it is shut.

@file underworld/escape
@encounter 6

= the gate
@continue
Black basalt, hewn in courses, fitted without mortar.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
Giants are carved either side, each with a single eye,
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
and over the lintel an eye is cut, half-lidded, watching.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
Red light bleeds under the door, and the heat comes with it.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]

= the pounding
@continue
From far beyond and far below, a pounding: slow, even, without pause and without hurry.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
Not the sea. The sea has breath in it, a drawing-back, a thinking. This has none.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]

= where it goes
Beyond lie the Fomoire, and Balor’s halls of iron, where fire gives no comfort.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
The gate is sealed. It is no grief to leave it so.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
